# Journal 33 — Training-Free Looped Transformers — Lizhang Chen, Jonathan Li, Chen Liang, Ni Lao, Qiang Liu

Paper: Training-Free Looped Transformers — Lizhang Chen, Jonathan Li, Chen Liang, Ni Lao, Qiang Liu
arXiv: arXiv:2605.23872
Absorbed: 2026-11-24

Entry 33 — Paper 040 — Training-Free Looped Transformers, Lizhang Chen and Jonathan Li (co-first authors) with Chen Liang, Ni Lao and Qiang Liu (University of Texas at Austin), arXiv:2605.23872v1 — the tracker's second network taking-in, and the first pass to carry two changes in one build: the owed Chapter 50 addendum and a new chapter. The paper stood at rank 6 of the reference frontier, cited by Chapter 56's paper as the source of Looped-Qwen3; ranks 1-4 remain deferred for want of a politely fetchable source. It was fetched once from arXiv in HTML form and taken in: network stratum, no seal, non-sample. The work: recurrence is not a training decision — a lightweight wrapper loops a frozen checkpoint's contiguous mid-stack block at inference with no training, no new parameters and no architectural change, and the loop is principled by a reading: a pre-norm residual block is exactly one forward Euler step at h = 1 on its own residual field, so naive looping integrates to t = K, past the endpoint the post-loop layers were trained to receive, while the paper's strategies — damped sub-stepping, and a three-stage anchored Runge-Kutta scheme whose output is exactly a blend of the one-pass output and the refined endpoint — integrate the same t = 1 endpoint more finely. Block-mode for dense backbones, layer-mode for MoE, where block-mode spends itself on routing thrash; a depth fraction rule puts the window's centre in a narrow band and makes the wrapper a recipe rather than a search; and the failure log is the paper's honesty instrument — naive looping's perplexity collapse from 13 to over 1000, Anderson acceleration (optimal on contractive maps) the worst configuration found, the looped block measured not to be a contraction at all. The receipt-grade core ran the recomputation check a third time: Table 3 eight of thirteen deltas exact and five off by exactly one displayed unit, Table 4 all eighteen deltas exact, Section 3.5's percentages consistent, Table 9 eleven of fourteen exact at its own 0.001 grain, the two proofs (the field's telescoping; the blend's stage weights) read and sound with one cosmetic typo — and the finding of substance was again in the framing: Section 3.1 and Table 3's caption claim no per-cell search over position, K or strategy, Section 3.4 calls Table 3 the best configuration per family, and Appendix P documents a per-cell search of about 720 pairs of which the survey cells 'are the result' — filed as a caveat at 58.1.4, the out-of-the-box claim rested on Table 4's pre-registered transfer run and the depth fraction rule instead, no False filing arising. Three exercises of the check have now yielded three different findings — a caption that overstated, prose looser than its tables, a protocol at odds with its captions — and the pattern is recorded in the detection list: in this stream the tables are more careful than the text that presents them. Integration: cluster AT extended for the second time rather than a new cluster founded — the trajectory manufactured by retrofit and integrated rather than read, the founding concept's own lineage line having already named this paper ('Chen et al.'), so 1.2.523 was argued NOT revised in the delta scroll — fourteen concepts 1.2.547-1.2.560, the foundation of an explicit Runge-Kutta method, two stated state machines, NI 0.0250, the axis judged no in writing, and the count reaching 560, so Restructuring Pass #25 fired inside the pass: four merge candidates weighed and held apart (sub-stepping into the blend, the two iteration modes into one, endpoint preservation into depth halving, the wrapper into the looped Transformer), no splits, no retirements, the next trigger set at Paper 045 or 580 concepts. The Chapter 50 addendum rides the same pass at 50.1.7: the build leg of the Alpöge artifact, completed clean on 2026-11-23 (175,187 compiled objects matching the source count, Main.olean newest, a re-run of lake build Main at exit 0, the five endpoints on exactly [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]), is recorded, and Will's ruling of 2026-11-21 is written into the record — 1.2.460 steps to True/verified only on independent-kernel checking of the five endpoints on a post-fix toolchain (4.36.0-class with nanoda and leanchecker-paranoid), not on the artifact's own 4.33.1 build, whose toolchain predates the kernel fixes of 4.34.0 (#14806, #14807, #14838) and is blind to that class; the original 50.1.3 stands as written, the addendum supersedes its step sentence and says why, the claim itself unmoved at Unknown/attributed, and the registry's only change under the addendum is the addendum's own entry. Author check #48 ran on all five names — the paper read entire and searched, its 102 references read, the web, Will's Twitter archive of 33,063 tweets (whose single 'looped transformer' occurrence is a liked post about a different work, itself queue rank 15) — and found no evidence. The registry's counts were taken from the extractor, never by hand — a hand count of Table 9's grain was wrong by one during the check and the script's figure stands — and the addendum, the drawing paragraph and the new chapter were each grepped for in the built phext before closing. Re-proof ran on ni-knight, not the hub: the splice verified 1,397 entries inside currentRegistry, fresh project and standing copy both built clean with all exits 0, and Mvo.currentRegistry_accurate depends on [propext] alone in both. The phextura shadow replayed the transaction exactly (no differing scrolls; the log's NI agreed with the canonical figure) and validated green with the pass's own conversion report passed explicitly; the Singular audit closed at residual 0, after one correction of form — the drawing at 1.4.1 is the counts paragraph only, and the first Phase B draft, written from a summary's paraphrase rather than the held file, was caught by its own anchor failing and rewritten from Paper 039's actual text. Registry after: 1,397 entries — True 542 (440 by stipulation