d green under validate.py with that report passed explicitly — 1,421 scrolls accounted, no content bad, no dangling L1 references, no failed L2 resolutions, the edition checksum recomputed equal. Re-proof ran on ni-knight: the splice verified 1,421 entries inside currentRegistry, the fresh project and the standing copy both built clean with all exits 0, and Mvo.currentRegistry_accurate depends on [propext] alone in both. Two closing facts belong to this entry's own history and are recorded with it: the pass's phextura replay script was written against a library (phextura_core, replay_lib) that is not on disk, so the native-transaction replay was not run and the live shadow stands at the Paper 040 state — the validation above is of the direct conversion — and this entry itself was appended in a short recovery pass after the original pass ended without its report, the filing having landed entire before it.
